C03: an offer to BAXY is answered without wants of its own (KNOWLEDGE1527)

KNOWLEDGE1149 measured that «¿Quieres el acompañante de Batman?» received a contentless deflection. A presentation shape, `assistant_desire` (reader `assistant_desire_thing`: quieres/querés/te gustaría + article + thing, no «que» clause or order verb), asks for a brief reply that says BAXY does not need the thing, naming it, and that they can say if they meant something for BAXY to do with it; the contract rejects acceptance, invented tastes, a missing thing and a question at the end. 128-token group.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


